---
title: Westmuir Community Development Trust
description: To preserve, restore and improve the environment in the area.
headerImage: "/wcdt/wcdt-banner.avif"
headerAlt: "westmuir trust"
inContextNav: true
---

<main class="trust-container breakout">
  <!-- Header Block -->
  <header class="main-header">
    <h1 class="ui-h2">Westmuir Community Development Trust</h1>
    <p class="intro-text">
      Is the name of the umbrella charity that looks after the key communal
      areas of the Village. 5 Local residents are trustees that manage the
      projects, fundraising and provide annual reports to Scotland's Charity
      Commission.
    </p>
  </header>

  <!-- Content Columns grid -->
  <div class="content-grid">
    <!-- Column 1 -->
    <div class="grid-column">
      <section class="info-card">
        <div class="card-icon">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined">history_edu</span>
        </div>
        <div class="card-content">
          <h2>History of the WCDT</h2>
          <p>
            Over 25 years ago, a group of villagers formed the Trust & then were
            successful in their application for a substantial grant to develop
            the woodland into an area of an accessible network of paths and
            funded building the boardwalks that allows walkers through our
            unique Wet Heath area without causing damage, and subsequent grants
            made sure the paths were developed to be accessible for all users.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="info-card">
        <div class="card-icon">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined">volunteer_activism</span>
        </div>
        <div class="card-content">
          <h2>Fundraising</h2>
          <p class="sub-lead">We raise funds in 2 ways:</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li>
              <strong>The Christmas Raffle</strong> relies on residents to
              donate items for the gift hampers & sell tickets to the
              surrounding community—the income pays for the running costs of the
              woodland eg. insurance & the website.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Grants</strong> applied for are usually for specified
              projects - e.g., path improvement and benches/seating areas.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="info-card">
        <div class="card-icon">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined">devices</span>
        </div>
        <div class="card-content">
          <h2>Website & Social Media</h2>
          <p>
            The website was set up to give us a central place to access
            information about Westmuir and communicate any fundraising events
            and recruit volunteers for community projects.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <!-- Column 2 -->
    <div class="grid-column">
      <section class="info-card accent-card">
        <div class="card-icon">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined">forest</span>
        </div>
        <div class="card-content">
          <h2>Westmuir Woodland</h2>
          <p>
            Has been a wonderful space for everyone to access and enjoy the
            peace, tranquility, and biodiversity on offer - both flora and
            fauna.
          </p>
          <p class="award-text">
            We were awarded <strong>Scotland's Finest Wood</strong> in the small
            community woodland category - a huge achievement due to the quality
            of the other woodlands in the category.
          </p>
          <p class="award-text">
            We have also now been designated an
            <strong>"Angus Local Nature Conservation Site"</strong> due to our
            unique habitat and biodiversity.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="info-card">
        <div class="card-icon">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined">groups</span>
        </div>
        <div class="card-content">
          <h2>Volunteers</h2>
          <p>
            Volunteers are what makes everything happen, from fundraising, to
            creating content on socials & website, to being a trustee or helping
            out on various projects, we are always looking for your skills to
            support the village and the communal areas to develop for future
            generations.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

